  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Victims of Human Trafficking to Receive Psychosocial Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main beneficiaries of the project are victims of trafficking (VOTs), mainly female victims of sexual exploitation, the shelters run by the NGOs &#x2018;Rahmdillik&#x2019;, &#x2018;Oydin Nur&#x2019; and &#x2018;Istiqlol Avlodi&#x2019; and key GoU entities, including National Commission on Countering Human Trafficking and Labour Exploitation, National Gender Commission, and Ministry of Internal Affairs. IOM will work with these NGOs and Government partners to enhance access to psychosocial services for VOTs at their shelters. Other NGOs and the relevant GoU entities will be involved in the advocacy workshops to improve the capacity of identification of VOTs who are in need of psychosocial support and referral of these VOTs to the shelters.</narrative>
  </description>
